# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit .env.
#
# Nothing here is required: `npm run dev` works with an empty file.
#
# These are development settings only. In production the same values are
# compiled into the server bundle by CDK (see `infra/lib/website-stack.ts`),
# because a Lambda@Edge function cannot have environment variables. The
# deployment's own settings live in `cdk.json`, not here: the pipeline builds
# from a clean checkout and has no .env.
#
# Secrets do not belong in this file's production counterpart at all. If the
# site ever needs one, store it as an SSM SecureString and give the server its
# *path*; the value is then read at run time and never enters a bundle.

# Deliver contact form messages through SES instead of printing them to the
# terminal. Needs AWS credentials in your shell and an address verified in SES.
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=
SES_REGION=us-east-1
